cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "PlatePrep: browser-based preparation of settlement-plate imagery for annotation platforms"
version: 1.0.4
date-released: 2026-08-15
license: CC-BY-4.0
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/The-Bioe-Project/plateprep"
url: "https://www.projetobioe.com/plateprep.html"
abstract: >-
  Single-file, bilingual (English/Portuguese) browser application that prepares
  settlement-plate campaign photographs for annotation: campaign metadata from
  EXIF/GPS with optional weather retrieval, per-plate triage, four-corner homography
  cropping at fixed physical scale, and output of annotation-ready images, an
  import-ready metadata table, a triage map and a crop manifest recording the four
  source corners of every crop.
keywords:
  - benthic image analysis
  - biofouling
  - settlement plates
  - homography
  - percent cover
  - point count
  - image preprocessing
  - CoralNet
authors:
  - family-names: Galembeck
    given-names: Eduardo
    affiliation: "Institute of Biology, University of Campinas (Unicamp), Campinas, SP, Brazil"
  - family-names: Schlosser
    given-names: "Carolina F."
    affiliation: "Centre for Marine Biology, University of São Paulo (CEBIMar/USP), São Sebastião, SP, Brazil"
